---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
];
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About High Voltage Insights — an independent editorial publication covering HV cable termination technology."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <h1>About High Voltage Insights</h1>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    High Voltage Insights is an independent editorial publication covering HV termination
    technology — materials, methods, and standards — for engineers, asset managers, and
    procurement teams who want depth: material chemistry, test data, failure modes, and
    named projects, not marketing copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial format</h2>
  <p>
    We write in an editorial, trade-press format rather than a sales format: no pricing,
    no calls to request a quote, no product pages. The content is reported and written to
    the same standard we'd hold an outside technical publication to. Where we cite a
    specific company's work — a project, a testing method, a termination system — it's
    because it's directly relevant to the technical point being made, cited from public
    reporting and standards documentation.
  </p>

  <h2>Related coverage</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://droppercable.com">Plug &amp; Go High Voltage</a> is a separate
    publication focused specifically on offshore wind dropper cables and connection
    systems. The two sites cover adjacent but distinct topics — dropper cables and
    array-side connections there, termination technology and field grading here — and
    occasionally link to each other where a topic genuinely overlaps.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
  <p>
    We write for engineers, asset managers, and procurement teams who want specifics —
    material chemistry, test standards, failure modes, named projects — cited from public
    reporting and standards documentation where we reference them, not marketing copy.
  </p>
</Layout>
